  "claim": "Lommel differential equation was developed by the German physicist who was the doctoral advisor to another German Physicist who identified the Stark effect.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Eugen von Lommel. Sentence: Eugen Cornelius Joseph von Lommel (19 March 1837, Edenkoben – 19 June 1899, Munich) was a German physicist.\nPage: Eugen von Lommel. Sentence: He is notable for the Lommel polynomial, the Lommel function, the Lommel–Weber function, and the Lommel differential equation.\nPage: Eugen von Lommel. Sentence: He is also notable as the doctoral advisor of the Nobel Prize winner Johannes Stark.\nPage: Johannes Stark. Sentence: Johannes Stark (] , 15 April 1874 – 21 June 1957) was a German physicist and Physics Nobel Prize laureate.\nPage: Johannes Stark. Sentence: He is known for identifying the Stark effect, and was later closely involved with the \"Deutsche Physik\" movement under the Nazi regime.",
