        "original_id": "8874870c-c07f-5e79-88e8-5f0953d1515f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugen von Lommel, Johannes Stark\n- Roles: German physicists, doctoral advisor, Physics Nobel Prize laureate\n- Concepts: Lommel polynomial, Lommel function, Lommel–Weber function, Lommel differential equation, Stark effect, Deutsche Physik\n- Places: Edenkoben, Munich\n\nFacts:\n- Eugen von Lommel was born on 19 March 1837 in Edenkoben and died on 19 June 1899 in Munich.\n- Eugen von Lommel was a German physicist.\n- Eugen von Lommel is notable for the Lommel polynomial, the Lommel function, the Lommel–Weber function, and the Lommel differential equation.\n- Eugen von Lommel was the doctoral advisor of Johannes Stark.\n- Johannes Stark was born on 15 April 1874 and died on 21 June 1957.\n- Johannes Stark was a German physicist and a Physics Nobel Prize laureate.\n- Johannes Stark is known for identifying the Stark effect.\n- Johannes Stark was later closely involved with the Deutsche Physik movement under the Nazi regime.",
